# SonoJS docs — featured (green bullet)

In `lib/docs-nav.ts`, `featured: true` shows a **bright green** sidebar bullet (`SidebarNavBullet`).

## When to set `featured: true`

Mark a docs page if it is **commonly used / core** for building UIs — something most apps reach for early:

- Primitives: Button, Input, Checkbox, Select, Switch, Label
- Structure: Card, Accordion, Tabs, Dialog / Alert Dialog, Sheet
- Data: Avatar, Table / Data Table, Calendar / Date Picker, Combobox
- Cross-cutting docs that matter for the product (e.g. Direction)

## When NOT to feature

- Niche / secondary: Bubble, Attachment, Context Menu, Carousel, Code Block, Collapsible, Command palette variants, Button Group (unless it becomes a primary pattern)
- Do not feature every new component — green should stay sparse so it signals importance

## Checklist (new docs component)

1. Add the page to `lib/docs-nav.ts` (alpha in its group).
2. If it matches the “commonly used / core” bar above → `featured: true`.
3. If unsure → leave featured off; easier to promote later than to dilute the green dots.
